UID:82b36023fe3a3fba@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260922T051006Z
SEQUENCE:2026092205
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Coffee ***\nArabian
  Coffee — Costume (you provide): Flesh-tone Camisole Leotard\, No tigh
 ts\; Shoes: Flesh-tone Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascar
 a Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Shee
 t:\n• Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin to
 ne eye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n
 • Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes
  (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n
 • Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to
  apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n
 • Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil
  (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDa
 ncers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\n
 Costume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while chan
 ging to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet A
 rkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no ma
 tter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the flo
 or\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting 
 on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clea
 n\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up w
 hile in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-
 up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perf
 ume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned
  to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in 
 costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from t
 heir assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby p
 ins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return 
 all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all
  updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack marker
 s\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costume
 s.
